WEBVTT

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.610
Let's eat!

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:16.490
Ryo! You need to put your legs into it!

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:17.490
Okay...

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:24.410
If you keep this up, you'll never be ready for field day in two weeks!

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.410
Now, let's practice serving.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:30.380
I'll show you how, so watch closely.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.670
Okay? This is how you serve!

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.680
There's no way I can do that!

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:49.190
Kirin, you're way too demanding!

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:50.900
Don't give me that!

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.610
Weren't you the one who asked for a crash course before field day?

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.320
Well, yeah, but...

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:58.990
I hate field day.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:00.570
I really, really hate it.

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.570
If I play ball sports, I always end up with a nosebleed.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.830
If I run, I always sprain an ankle.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:12.000
There's probably even more that I've repressed.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.460
Field day is scary!

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:16.840
It's really, really terrifying!

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.720
I wouldn't worry <i>that</i> much about it...

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.340
I mean, you're not athletic at <i>all</i>,

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:27.100
but there's nothing wrong with that.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:32.190
It gives me something I can help you out with, for one.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:38.400
With everything that's happened lately, I've learned to rely on you more.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.780
Yeah, that's it! I don't mind doing more at all!

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.200
I'll do anything, even dishwashing!

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:47.830
I'm up to a 45% survival rate there!

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:54.630
Well, maybe after you've had a little more practice.

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:59.420
Your field day's on a Sunday, right?

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:02.180
So you'll be skipping cram school.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.760
Don't worry. You can still come over.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.010
Of course!

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:11.930
We've only got two weeks left to whip you into shape!

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:14.480
Without the whip, if that's okay.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:18.230
Oh, by the way, are you going to need a lunch for field day?

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:18.940
Well...

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.940
Actually, my school provides meals.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:24.450
Really? That's great!

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:26.200
Kirin?

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:30.750
I'm honestly not confident that I'd be able to put together a boxed lunch yet.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:34.580
Oh, were you going to make lunch for me?

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:39.050
I even thought of a menu!

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:40.590
See? Doesn't it sound fabulous?

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:44.930
That's a little <i>too</i> inventive.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:48.600
Really? I think the macaron with braised veggies is a long-overdue idea.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.970
The crispness of the macaron would really accentuate the rest of the dish.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:56.480
You making lunch, huh?

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:04.740
Beginning this year, you will be expected to bring your own lunches to field day.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.950
Guess I'll have to pick up something on the way.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:10.450
Yeah, I'll just grab whatever.

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:13.700
You're still growing, so you need to eat right.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:15.250
You need rice! Lots of rice!

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.040
So, what are you guys gonna do?

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.920
I'll have my mom make mine.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.710
Lucky you. My mom can't cook at all.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.930
All she ever does is reheat things.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:28.260
Mine too.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:30.390
What about you, Machiko?

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:32.520
I think I'll make my own.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:36.640
That sounds great! Your cooking's to die for!

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:38.150
What are you making?

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:41.270
Gourmet Chinese? A full-course French dinner?

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:44.320
Aw, now I want one.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:48.530
Weren't we talking about lunchboxes?

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:03.880
<i>Lunch for field day...</i>

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:16.430
You did well, Ryo.

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:19.190
But...

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.230
Here.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:23.360
I made you lunch.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:43.500
<i>I might be asking a bit too much.</i>

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:48.800
<i>But the first thing she cooked for me was so tasty.</i>

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:51.800
Here, Ryo! Try one!

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:55.430
No, I think I'll make it myself.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:10.570
<i>No matter how much she says she wants me to rely on her,</i>

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:17.080
<i>I don't want to be a burden.</i>

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:23.000
Hey, let's get ice cream on the way home!

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.380
Or maybe some meat buns.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:31.130
It's tough picking between warm and cold things at this time of year.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:35.100
Ryo?

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.230
Oh, meat buns? That sounds nice.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:57.490
I gotta go.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:14.090
Who put that there?

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:22.890
Ryo...

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:26.810
See you.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:27.900
Yeah, later!

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:32.190
We got out early today.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:34.780
So, now what? Want to go somewhere?

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:38.030
I've got plans, so I'm going straight home.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:39.290
Really?

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:41.950
I'll walk with you to the station, then.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.830
See you next week!

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:47.460
Kirin?

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:55.180
<i>A boxed lunch, huh?</i>

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:56.640
Yeah.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.970
Now that I think of it, my aunt—

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:03.640
Ryo's grandma—used to make sweet potato with lemon.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:06.060
S-Sweet potato with lemon?

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.650
I've never even heard of that.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:12.400
Shows how much you know.
It's one of the most popular boiled dishes.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:15.070
It sounds really good, though.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:18.700
I'll have to ask Dad to show me how to make it.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.080
Wait, why not me?

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:22.790
You know how?

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.170
Actually, yeah, go ahead and ask your father.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.090
Knew it.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:38.090
Hi!

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:41.760
You're early, Kirin.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.520
You should've texted me so I could pick you up.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.020
Ta-dah!

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:51.860
Wh-What are you doing?

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:59.820
Field day's tomorrow, you know!

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:02.030
We've got our work cut out for us!

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:03.540
Work?

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.540
Hurry up and get changed, Ryo!

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.040
Okay.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:15.300
Two breaths in, two breaths out! Keep it up!

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:22.300
All right! Let's keep this going
until we get to that supermarket!

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:23.310
Okay!

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:32.820
No stopping! We're not done yet!

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:36.030
You want to keep going inside?

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:40.070
But you're not supposed to run in shops!

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:41.280
Let's power walk, then!

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:47.750
What's on the list today?

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.790
Wieners and eggs,

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.460
fish sausage and cucumber!

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:59.550
<i>That's all the ingredients for the menu I wrote!</i>

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:08.310
<i>...I think.</i>

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:12.150
I can't believe you found my menu.

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:13.940
Why'd you try to hide it?

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:15.900
I told you I'd cook for you!

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:20.610
B-But you said you had a hard time with it.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:23.200
So you don't want me to cook for you?

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:26.120
I guess I'm not that good, but...

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:29.580
Of course I want you to cook for me!

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:34.340
All right!

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:37.090
I'm gonna cook up a storm for tomorrow! It'll be great!

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:39.880
Okay, next is bone-in chicken!

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:44.760
Wait, roaster chickens are too big! We need a fryer!

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:50.600
I can't hide anything from you, can I?

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:52.100
You know it!

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:55.810
You'll have to make a lot of different dishes, though.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:57.980
Are you sure you'll be okay?

00:11:57.980 --> 00:11:58.900
We've got this.

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:04.240
Practice is over, so we can make them together.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:05.450
That sounds great!

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:12.460
On the other hand, it'd be more exciting
if your lunch was a surprise, wouldn't it?

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:14.000
You're right.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:18.000
All right, I'll focus on the surprise!
You'd better get yourself ready for it!

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:25.640
<i>One way or another, it's going to be amazing.</i>

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:28.510
So, now that that's decided,
it's time for you to get some rest.

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:30.520
You've gotta be up early tomorrow.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:32.060
If there's anything you need a hand with—

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:33.390
I'll be fine.

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:37.690
It's wonderful that you care so much for other people,

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:40.900
but you don't have to wear yourself out for me.

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:42.860
Kirin...

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.910
Off you go! Chop, chop!

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:50.410
But...

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:58.000
K-Kirin?!

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:09.310
Make a cat's paw while chopping...

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:20.070
Next is the ninth-grade one-hundred-meter dash.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:23.820
<i>Kirin...</i>

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:31.790
<i>Kirin's cheering me on so much.</i>

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:35.080
<i>I can do this!</i>

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:38.710
<i>Yes...</i>

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:40.670
<i>I will...</i>

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:43.510
<i>become the wind!</i>

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:48.640
Wow, Machiko!

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:49.720
That's amazing!

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:53.720
Well, her expression is, at least.

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:57.600
She has the face of an Olympic sprinter in slow-mo...

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:58.810
but she's just slow.

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:00.310
Oh, she crossed the finish line.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.530
Sixth place.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:08.030
I did it, Kirin!

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:11.200
I managed not to fall over or sprain an ankle!

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:13.790
It's all because of you!

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:17.000
You did great, Machiko!

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.290
Thanks.

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:22.250
You look tired. Are you okay?

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:25.550
I was so nervous last night I could barely sleep.

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:30.550
<i>I was so excited about the boxed lunch,
and so worried that Kirin would hurt herself,</i>

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:38.060
<i>that I kept looking in all night even though I knew I wasn't supposed to peek.</i>

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:39.440
Machiko?

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.730
Oh, nothing.

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:42.560
Anyway, it's lunchtime.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:48.950
Yeah. We've all been looking forward to seeing what kind of amazing lunch you've brought.

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:51.490
An amazing lunch?

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:56.950
It sure is! I can't imagine anything better than this.

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:59.460
Really? C'mon, show us!

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:07.590
Huh?

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.340
Well, that's nothing special.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:11.720
Kind of a letdown.

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:13.760
Did you make this, Machiko?

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:17.810
Someone special made it for me.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:18.810
A boyfriend?!

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:20.140
Why assume that?

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:23.480
This had to have been made by a grownup.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:27.320
No one in middle school would plan out a menu like this!

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:29.610
H-Huh?

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:31.490
A lunch box?

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:33.910
Yeah, I made one for Ryo.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.490
You should have some too.

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:37.910
I'd love to, but I'll have to pass.

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:39.660
I have a sensitive stomach.

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:42.080
Don't worry about it!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.000
Dig right in!

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.630
I wasn't trying to—

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.510
That's a lot.

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:54.010
I kept messing them up.

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:57.180
And you want us to dispose of the evidence?

00:15:57.180 --> 00:16:02.520
I-It's not like that! They might look funny,
but they taste the same as the ones I made for Ryo!

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:07.270
Y-You can't make an omelette
without breaking a few eggs, right?

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:12.650
Or more than a few, in this case,
but that just means there's more to go around.

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:17.280
I'm not sure I get it, but okay.

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:20.910
Let's eat.

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:32.930
<i>Bone-in fried chicken.</i>

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:34.430
<i>Rolled omelettes.</i>

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.600
<i>Salisbury steak and a salad.</i>

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:41.980
<i>This is just like the menu I drew up!</i>

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:44.980
<i>Potatoes and ham fill out the salad.</i>

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:47.860
<i>The Salisbury steak is... mixed with cheese?</i>

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:52.240
<i>A nice variety for someone inexperienced at cooking.</i>

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:55.490
<i>Kirin is just like Grandma.</i>

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:57.700
What's the matter?

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:58.870
Oh, nothing.

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:01.870
Let's eat!

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:15.880
<i>The rolled omelettes are made with dried kelp.</i>

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:24.390
<i>The sweetness of the egg relaxes the heart,
accentuated by the sudden, soft saltiness.</i>

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:28.310
<i>Such an unlikely but wonderful contrast...</i>

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:30.400
<i>I can't stop eating!</i>

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:47.040
<i>And this juicy Salisbury steak,
with chopped cheese mixed in...</i>

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:51.460
<i>There's still a bit of texture left to the ground beef,</i>

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:56.970
<i>but the smooth cheese blends so well with its meatiness!</i>

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:05.140
There are so many wonderful things here that I've never tried, but they're all so good!

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:08.440
That sounds great! My mouth's watering!

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:10.230
Let's trade!

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:12.480
O-Okay...

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:14.990
Let's eat!

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.710
Huh? It really is nothing special.

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:31.880
More of a let-dow—

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:33.000
Shh!

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:36.760
<i>Kirin's cooking is the best!</i>

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:40.260
This broccoli looks great.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:43.640
Even the color coordination is impeccable!

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:44.260
Wait...

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:46.480
This is...

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:50.770
Here's your lunch.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:56.860
Grandma...

00:18:56.860 --> 00:19:00.610
You did well, Ryo.

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:03.280
Open wide for your gold medal, okay?

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:04.700
Sure!

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:11.170
It tastes good!

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:28.930
It tastes good.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:31.440
It really does taste good.

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:36.860
The soft, flaky natural sweetness of the sweet potato wraps around the refreshing tang of the lemon.

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:38.940
Together, they're like a refreshing spring breeze!

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:47.080
It really is the gold medal of boxed lunches!

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:54.170
M-Machiko?

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:57.090
You think she's one of <i>those</i> types, huh?

00:19:57.090 --> 00:20:01.340
I dunno, but she's really excited about something.

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:05.600
Remember to take your garbage home with you.

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:07.430
Later!

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:08.850
See you!

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:15.860
Huh, Kirin?

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:21.360
What's wrong?

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:24.030
I thought you were going home after cram school.

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:26.030
I'm sorry!

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:27.160
Huh?

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:30.120
I'm sorry I couldn't make a tasty lunch!

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:31.790
Kirin...

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:33.290
I double-checked!

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:35.040
I tried really hard!

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:39.420
But my first try was so bad that when I did a little bit better,

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:43.800
it tasted so much better by comparison that—

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:45.470
Hold on, Kirin.

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:51.310
I didn't even know what I was supposed to be aiming for,
so I just convinced myself that I'd done it right!

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:53.060
Kirin...

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:55.560
I thought it was delicious.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:57.060
You're just saying that!

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:02.490
But it really was.

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:09.490
The sweet potato with lemon wasn't even on my menu. How did you know?

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:12.620
Mom told me.

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:15.120
It was gentle and mild.

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:17.080
It tasted just like Grandma's.

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:19.750
Like happiness.

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:20.710
Really?

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:22.210
Yes.

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:25.840
I'm so glad!

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:32.430
Huh. I guess my stomach could handle it after all.

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:39.480
Thank you so much for everything today.

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:41.980
And for helping me practice, too.

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:43.190
Don't worry about it.

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:47.110
But hey, we don't need field day
to go for a run every now and then!

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:47.860
Huh?

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:50.120
It's good for your health!

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:53.370
There's my train. See you next week!

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:54.000
See you.

00:21:56.870 --> 00:21:59.130
It was great, Kirin.

00:22:00.790 --> 00:22:02.500
You're welcome!

00:23:42.940 --> 00:23:45.150
That smells great!

00:23:45.150 --> 00:23:48.990
Enjoying so many different ingredients at once is truly delectable.

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:52.320
I like the ones where you put all sorts of things inside the fried tofu.

00:23:52.320 --> 00:23:56.790
Mochi, shiitake mushrooms...
Maybe even rice crackers!

00:23:56.790 --> 00:24:01.160
Uh, Kirin, are you confusing it with mystery hot pot?

00:24:02.960 --> 00:24:05.710
Next time on Gourmet Girl Graffiti:

00:24:05.710 --> 00:24:07.960
Simmering and Steamy!
